# Direct delivery authority

- Read `AGENTS.md`, `delivery-harness/harness.yaml` and the elected project
  profile. Use only `DIRECT_CURSOR_DELIVERY`, `DIRECT_CODEX_DELIVERY` or
  `DESIGN_ONLY`; historical transport artifacts grant no active authority.
- Mutate, deliver and merge only from an exact task contract. Do not infer the
  current/next task from recency, branch names, Issues, PRs, commits, tests or
  chat history. Orientation may inspect Git truth without a new contract and
  must not create one or mutate; see `10-input-routing.mdc`.
- Routine bounded engineering, tests, Catalog/generated propagation, ordinary
  commits, non-force push, PR/review and CI are autonomous inside the stricter
  task contract. Do not ask for micro-approvals.
- Evaluate `OWNER_ATTENTION_GATE_V2` for material/external/user-only/destructive
  boundaries and merge. Failed machine checks are `DENY`.
- Cursor and Codex have the same guarded merge right: only after exact-head CI
  and the exact owner phrase for the unchanged PR/head. The owner never clicks
  GitHub Merge; the elected direct agent merges.
- Git is working project memory. Cloud bundle/Project Instruction is
  `OWNER_MANAGED_OPTIONAL_EXPORT`; never request replacement or smoke.
- Tests, PR, CI or merge do not by themselves establish semantic acceptance,
  canonical `DONE`, alpha or cashflow.
